# my_bot serial device names. Generated by scripts/setup_udev.sh on 2026-09-08T16:06:54+08:00.
# Regenerate after swapping hardware or moving a device to another USB port.
#
# CORRECTED BY HAND 2026-09-08 (Day 1 §5.1): the two KERNELS values were the
# wrong way round -- `make udev` was answered with the adapters swapped, and
# nothing about that fails loudly, because both are 10c4:ea60 reporting the
# same non-unique serial `0001`.
#
# Which is which, measured on the hardware rather than assumed:
#
#   1-2.2.1 (was ttyUSB1) -- ESP32.  Quiet until spoken to; opening it prints
#                            the ROM banner "ets Jul 29 2019 12:21:46" and then
#                            "# boot reset=1 encoders=ok" at 57600. `e` answers
#                            "0 0", `r` answers "OK".
#   1-2.2.4 (was ttyUSB0) -- YDLidar X2. Streams ~4.5 kB/s unprompted with
#                            0xAA55 frame headers at 115200, and never stops.
#
# Re-verify after any replug with:  scripts/encoder_report.py --seconds 2
# It refuses to run against a port that streams, which is exactly this fault.

# esp32 has no unique serial -- matched by USB port. Keep it in this port.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", KERNELS=="1-2.2.1", SYMLINK+="esp32", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
# ydlidar has no unique serial -- matched by USB port. Keep it in this port.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", KERNELS=="1-2.2.4", SYMLINK+="ydlidar", GROUP="dialout", MODE="0660"
